                                                "sense_id": "4dacb909-c8f9-359a-b77b-ecea65d895fc",
                                                "text": "He had taken the wife to his raw new palace in San Diego, where she and her people occupied a wing of great price, and Cheyne, in a veranda-room, between a secretary and a typewriter, who was also a telegraphist, toiled along wearily from day to day."
